      "notes": "All claims are well-grounded in their cited evidence. Tier assignments are appropriate: stated claims draw from policy text, measurables from parliamentary library and census data, projections clearly labelled. The 'mixed' direction is genuinely supported by claims on both sides (minor benefit to some UK nationals vs. risks of increased homelessness and private rent pressure), not a false balance \u2014 the evidence does point in genuinely different directions for different groups even if the net supply effect is near-zero. The E27 claim is slightly unusual \u2014 the quote comes from a summary/analysis source (365invest/shelter) rather than the party itself, but it is correctly tier-labelled as stated about what the policy says and contrasted with current law, so not a material issue. The magnitude (minor) and time_horizon (this-parliament) are plausible given legal uncertainty and the small share of tenancies that would actually be affected. No lever leakage, no party identity smuggling, no false balance detected."
    },
